1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,531
In 1999, an engineer bought over

2
00:00:02,531 --> 00:00:05,143
12,000 cups of chocolate pudding...

3
00:00:05,143 --> 00:00:06,753
just for the BARCODES.

4
00:00:06,753 --> 00:00:09,319
David Phillips spotted a Healthy Choice deal:

5
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:11,767
mail in barcodes, get free airline miles.

6
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:13,810
10 barcodes, 500 miles.

7
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:15,789
Mail them early, and the miles DOUBLED.

8
00:00:15,789 --> 00:00:18,181
Then he found the cheapest barcode in the store:

9
00:00:18,181 --> 00:00:20,234
pudding. 25 cents a cup.

10
00:00:20,234 --> 00:00:22,126
He cleared out store after store...

11
00:00:22,126 --> 00:00:24,365
and had a manager order more cases.

12
00:00:24,365 --> 00:00:25,723
The problem?

13
00:00:25,723 --> 00:00:28,034
12,000 barcodes to peel off.

14
00:00:28,034 --> 00:00:29,988
By hand. Before the deadline.

15
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:32,519
His fix: the Salvation Army.

16
00:00:32,519 --> 00:00:34,632
Volunteers peeled the barcodes...

17
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:36,584
and the pudding went to people in need.

18
00:00:36,584 --> 00:00:38,848
He spent about $3,000.

19
00:00:38,848 --> 00:00:41,343
Healthy Choice sent him over a MILLION miles.

20
00:00:41,343 --> 00:00:44,129
The donation even got him a tax write-off.

21
00:00:44,129 --> 00:00:45,813
And Hollywood put his pudding plan

22
00:00:45,813 --> 00:00:47,570
into an Adam Sandler movie.

23
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:50,364
Every 25-cent cup earned about 100 miles.

24
00:00:50,364 --> 00:00:51,467
He wasn't buying dessert.

25
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:53,394
He was buying a MILLION miles...

26
00:00:53,394 --> 00:00:55,050
and he gave the pudding to charity.
